nk that there has to be certain qualifications for what constitutes planethood.  Just because I don&#39;t believe Pluto should be considered a planet doesn&#39;t mean I can&#39;t marvel at its celestial splendor, however.  On another note, one that affects you much greater than myself, have you ever heard of the supervolcano underneath Yellowstone National Park?&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FOn3wkehluk</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115620219784406660/comments/default/9107811873837584530'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/115620219784406660/comments/default/9107811873837584530'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/why-not-dozen-planets-or-more-updated.html?showComment=1234392600000#c9107811873837584530' title=''/><author><name>Josh</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/08412892387498489410</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2006/08/why-not-dozen-planets-or-more-updated.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-115620219784406660' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/115620219784406660' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-880820851"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="February 11, 2009 at 3:50 PM"/></entry></feed>